/*
  LinearSidebar.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0174 · LinearSidebar (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Keys mirror the web source
  (components/layout/sidebar/LinearSidebar.tsx) `nav.*` namespace VERBATIM — the `t(key, default)` calls
  and the per-row `navLabel` labels — so every Swift literal routes through the facade fallback and the
  sources hold no hardcoded English. `{{page}}` / `{{count}}` slots are filled by
  LinearSidebarInterpolation (the native peer of i18next interpolation).

  Two keys have no literal web string because the web owns the filter STATE but renders its typing surface
  upstream and leaves an empty `<nav>` for the no-data case; the native peer realizes both (a filter field
  + a friendly empty state), so each gets a localizable key here.

  The "linearSidebar.sample.*" entries back the DEBUG-only inspector + previews; they are never shipped.

  These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept
  in a per-surface table ("LinearSidebar") so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings.
*/

/* --- Shipped copy (verbatim from the web nav.* namespace) --- */
"nav.sidebar" = "Sidebar navigation";
"nav.favorites" = "Favorites";
"nav.filterNoMatch" = "No matches.";
